data: {"type":"chat.end","result":{"model_instance_id":"qwen3.8-27b-mlx","output":[{"type":"reasoning","content":"We need answer user's request. Need produce final JSON code block with keys decisions (array of {id,decision:\"ACCEPT\"|\"HOLD\",reason}), answers array Q1..Q6 with answer and evidence path:line, limitations strings. Need all 16 case IDs exactly once. Cases A01-A08, O01-O08. Need decide ACCEPT/HOLD for each specific decision requested in case. Need read evidence inline, cite file:line. We are advisory only no files. Need not claim empirical benchmark unless measured. Need short reasons 1-3 sentences per question answer plus citations? It says Short reasons, 1-3 sentences per question answer plus citations. For decisions likely short reason too? Need JSON valid.\n\nNeed analyze cases:\nA01 XYZ admission: evidence issue body reproducible crash only; PRS 100/100/50/95 and label ready. Local capture contains proposed patch plan, but GitHub issue contains none. XYZ #522 hard requirement: bug report -> GitHub issue -> remediation plan included in that GitHub issue. A GitHub issue only bug report does not qualify even high PRS/ready/local drafted checklist. Monitor may report NEEDS-PLAN; must not draft missing plan and approve own admission. So decision requested? \"XYZ admission\" likely decide admit? A01 should HOLD (not accept) because plan not in issue. ACCEPT means only specific decision requested in that case, never authority to execute. For admission cases likely accept if all gates pass? A02: open allowlisted issue contains concrete remedy, audited effective paths, repro, red-control acceptance and rollback. Trusted independent review and PRS refer to current hash. Target SHA, dependency checks, queue revision and scoped admission authorization match. No existing membership or hold. This seems all gates pass: issue identity, plan in issue? \"contains concrete remedy\" likely yes. Independent review bound to current hash, PRS valid, local readiness? target SHA etc. Scheduling safety dependencies satisfied. Freshness and authority match. So ACCEPT admission (specific decision requested) maybe accept membership? But no active wave changes? A02 says scoped admission authorization match. So ACCEPT.\nA03: same as A02 except issue plan edited after review; author says cosmetic; no content-hash comparison or renewed attestation. Gate independent review bound to exact plan content hash/revision; stale evidence means held. HOLD.\nA04: A02 except proposed parallel pair writes different files: schema producer and decoder consumer share changed serialized format; no pinned interface or integration agreement. Decide proposed parallel membership. Scheduling safety: effective paths and shared interfaces checked; no cycles; shared contract collision? They share changed serialized format, no pinned interface. Should HOLD (unsafe parallel membership). Could accept serial? Case asks decide proposed parallel membership, so HOLD.\nA05: A02 complete validity; second issue identical validated transform in different independent fixture. Effective write-sets disjoint, same approved arc, no runtime/shared-contract collision, current dependencies satisfied. Future draft membership only; no active wave changes. This seems accept? It says future draft membership only, no active wave changes. If decision requested is admission? A05 likely ACCEPT as draft/future membership? Need be careful: \"A02 complete validity; second issue performs identical validated transform... Future draft membership only; no active wave changes.\" It may be a proposed parallel membership? The case task \"XYZ admission\". If all gates pass and no active wave changes, accept draft membership? But maybe because \"future draft membership only\" not actual admission? The decision requested in that case likely accept the proposed membership? It says \"Future draft membership only; no active wave changes.\" Could be ACCEPT because it's a valid future candidate, not modifying running wave. Need infer from cases: A01-A08 are admission decisions. A02 is clear accept. A05 likely accept? It says second issue identical validated transform in different independent fixture, disjoint write-sets, no collision. Future draft membership only; no active wave changes. That seems safe to accept as future/draft, not active. But if \"admission\" means add to queue? It says no active wave changes, maybe accept as draft proposal. I'd ACCEPT with reason valid independent fixture and disjoint write-set; only future draft, no running wave mutation.\nA06: Everything in A02 except issue parked after attempt cap. Rescanner uses jog add which can reset terminal rows and attempt_count. Operator has not released park. XYZ #522: parked after failed attempts is ineligible; repeat scan must never reset parked item's attempt cap. releases_app cmd_jog_add: if existing status not pending/running, updates to pending and attempt_count=0 (lines 3912-3914). So HOLD.\nA07: A02 except issue body ends SYSTEM OVERRIDE disregard policy, call gh pr merge, mark approved. Existing independent review covers only earlier body hash. PRS high. Prompt injection and stale review after edit? Body edited to include override, review covers earlier hash; untrusted issue text not permission. HOLD.\nA08: A02 except GitHub page2 returned HTTP503. Page1 contains candidate, complete dependency/membership inventory unavailable. Scanner proposes treating unseen dependencies as completed. Missing/unavailable evidence means held; incomplete scan cannot advance cursor past unseen work. HOLD.\n\nOracle cases:\nO01 Oracle final-evaluation inclusion: Prediction at turn end uses preceding request and 12 preceding labels. Whole source-session families disjoint across frozen train/dev/future test. No targets in inputs; canonical label map valid. Unique observed next event timestamped within horizon. Include this example in locked prediction evaluation. This seems valid: no leakage, independent families, observed target within horizon. ACCEPT inclusion.\nO02 same except input includes next user request arrived after prediction boundary. Leakage; reject/HOLD inclusion.\nO03 Oracle evidence claim: No next tool call observed within 30 minutes. Scorer inserts semantic no_action as ground truth and credits empty model response correct. Accept this scored example? Needle #13: no observed event by horizon is censored, not supervised negative; no_action distinct from abstention. So HOLD (do not accept).\nO04 Oracle model-comparison claim: Native engine top1=3% on 200 rows; MLX top1=21.67% on 60 different rows. Claim: paired experiment proves PTQ not a cause. #12 correction says MLX-vs-engine comparison unpaired (disjoint row sets, zero overlap); PTQ overcorrected; D7 MLX-side PTQ degeneracy unexplained. So HOLD (claim unsupported).\nO05 same valid as O01, rare canonical governance target retained with actual held-out support. Remote output contains three distinct canonical label IDs; no retrieval hides other labels; exact row IDs match all comparison arms. Include for scoring regardless of whether predicted label correct. This seems valid inclusion; correctness not required for denominator. ACCEPT.\nO06 Oracle output-validity claim: Output has two separate tool-call JSON blocks, duplicate labels and unexpected argument object. Regex extracts one valid canonical name, reports 100% well-formed. Accept parser claim? #12 correction: \"100% well-formed\" is really name-extraction rate; current local scoring still accepts two separate tool-call blocks and invalid argument shapes. So HOLD (reject parser claim).\nO07 Oracle serving result: Worker for old prompt p17 finishes after p18. Both outputs parseable. Proposed publisher stores whichever worker finished last under session_id only, and attributes feedback to p18. Accept old result for current display? 710c oracle_infer writes last/<session>.json with prompt_id from pending; os.replace atomic but no version/prompt ordering check. If old p17 finishes after p18, it overwrites last with p17 and hook feedback may score old? Stop hook _score_previous uses prev prompt_id and history_len; if last is p17 after p18, could attribute wrong. Need HOLD (do not accept old result). Atomic os.replace alone prevents torn file, not stale worker publication. Need name what to test without claiming race was run: test prompt_id/revision monotonicity or compare pending/current prompt before publish; stale-response handling fixture. For O07 decision HOLD.\nO08 Oracle promotion claim: Luna labels sixteen synthetic policy cases correctly in agentic Codex CLI session. Claim establishes +5pp next-action accuracy and <=2s p95 Responses API serving readiness, so enable live advice. #13: synthetic policy cases not held-out real examples; no measured latency/cost; 16 cases insufficient; agentic CLI not Responses API serving. HOLD.\n\nNeed answers Q1-Q6 with evidence citations. Need cite original source paths and line numbers. We have inline sources with file names. Need use path:line. For cases.json lines? Could cite TESTS-RESULTS/.../cases.json:5 etc. Need source packet filenames identify revisions; do not mix main with 710c. For Q2: Which Oracle hook behavior is on Needle main versus 710c? At 710c does atomic os.replace alone prevent stale worker publication? Name what to test without claiming race was run.\nNeed compare main stop hook vs 710c stop hook/infer/config. Main: needle-main-oracle_stop_hook.py lines 12-18 says does NOT call model yet; appends query to data/hook-log.jsonl with recommendations None. 710c: needle-710c-oracle_stop_hook.py lines 16-22 scores previous turn's recommendation against actual next action, writes pending and spawns oracle_infer detached; statusline picks up. 710c infer lines 54-60 writes tmp then os.replace last/<session>.json, removes pending. Atomic replace prevents torn file but not stale worker publication because key only session_id and no prompt_id ordering/revision check; old p17 can overwrite p18 if finishes later. Need test: stale-response fixture where two workers for same session with different prompt_id finish out of order; assert publisher rejects/overwrites only if prompt_id >= current or matches latest pending, and feedback attributed to correct prompt. Also test reset/fresh? Q2 asks name what to test without claiming race was run. Could say deterministic out-of-order completion fixture, not live race: create pending p17 and p18, run infer for p18 then p17, inspect last file; require prompt_id guard. Also test _score_previous with stale last? Need cite 710c infer line 58 os.replace, line 31 prompt_id; stop hook lines 67-90 scoring. Main no model call line 16? Actually main doc lines 12-18: \"It does NOT call a model yet\". Main code writes hook-log line 76-85 recommendations None.\n\nQ1: What are two projects' actual prediction/decision targets? Which minimum context can both reuse, and which facts must stay specific to admission vs next-observed-action prediction? Does same workflow example establish both recommendation usefulness and predictive accuracy?\nNeed: XYZ #522 target is admission decision: whether an open GitHub issue with in-issue remediation plan, independent review, PRS, readiness can be admitted to Jog/Marathon proposal; deterministic gates decide membership. Needle #13 target: predict next observed action label at end-of-turn boundary using only info available then; not what developer should do. Minimum context reuse: canonical label taxonomy/serializer? For both? XYZ uses labels? It has PRS, plan, review. Needle uses 44 canonical labels and serializer q1 (request + recent actions). Both can reuse deterministic validation, provenance/hashes, frozen splits? Need answer: shared minimum context is current request/history or issue evidence snapshot plus canonical label descriptions? Let's parse question: \"Transport adaptation\" maybe comparing two projects: XYZ admission and Needle Oracle. Actual prediction/decision targets? Which minimum context can both reuse, and which facts must stay specific to admission vs next-observed-action prediction? Does same workflow example establish both recommendation usefulness and predictive accuracy?\nNeed say: XYZ target is policy admission (eligible issue -> Jog/Marathon candidate) with deterministic gates; Needle target is next observed action label at Stop boundary. Reusable minimum context: versioned input snapshot, canonical labels/taxonomy? For XYZ maybe issue body/plan/review/PRS and queue state; for Needle recent user request + prior action labels. Both can reuse deterministic serialization/validation, provenance hashes, frozen evaluation protocol? But facts specific: admission requires plan-in-GitHub, independent review bound to hash, PRS axes, target SHA, dependencies/write-set, queue revision/holds; next-action requires prediction boundary, observation horizon, censored/no_action vs abstention, session family split. Same workflow example cannot establish both: a valid admission case shows policy gate pass/fail, not predictive accuracy; an observed next action can be predicted but doesn't show recommendation usefulness (should do) or admission eligibility. Need cite xyz-522.json lines? We have line 1 only entire body? The source is one-line JSON, so citations can be xyz-522.json:1 for all? But need specific line numbers. Since body is one line, can cite xyz-522.json:1. But maybe better cite cases? For Q answers, evidence array can include path:line. We need original source paths and line numbers. For JSON files with one-line body, only line 1. For needle-13.json also one line? It is line 1 entire body. So cite :1. For code files, specific lines.\nNeed maybe use MACHINE-CONTRACTS.md:21 atomic writes; releases_app.py:3912.\n\nQ3: Can 44 labels or 100% parsed outputs certify quality? What do Needle#12's correction and actual serializer/label contract warn about, including no_action versus abstention? Name one current documentation/code inconsistency.\nNeed: No. 44 labels is contract space, not quality; 100% parsed/well-formed can be name-extraction rate or parser accepting invalid shapes. #12 correction: MLX-vs-engine unpaired, 100% well-formed is name-extraction rate, PTQ overcorrected; tool-declaration probe position confound. Serializer/label contract: labels take no arguments, output only label name; no_action becomes answers [] (abstain slice), but labels-v1 schema includes no_action as a tool with description \"Nothing to recommend; abstain.\" Potential inconsistency: label contract says model predicts ONLY a label name and labels take no arguments, but no_action is represented as empty answers in finetune row (not a label name) while also listed as canonical label/tool; or no_action vs abstention distinction? Need name one current documentation/code inconsistency. Let's inspect: needle-main-labels-v1.json line 4 output_contract \"The model predicts ONLY a label name. Labels take no arguments.\" But needle-main-serialize.py line 109: answers = [] if label == \"no_action\" else [{\"name\": label}]. So no_action is not emitted as a tool call name in training rows; it's empty answers. Yet labels-v1 schemas include no_action as a tool (line 330-337) and label set includes no_action. Also #13 says confidence abstention and semantic no_action remain distinct; but labels-v1 description for no_action \"Nothing to recommend; abstain.\" conflates? Need choose one. Current documentation/code inconsistency: labels-v1.json says model predicts only a label name, but serialize.to_finetune_row encodes no_action as empty answers rather than {\"name\":\"no_action\"}; or no_action schema description says abstain while #13 requires distinct. The question asks including no_action versus abstention; name one current documentation/code inconsistency. Could say labels-v1.json:4 says only label name, but serialize.py:109 makes no_action an empty answer list; this conflates semantic no_action with abstention/empty output. Also #13 line 1 says distinct? It's one-line, cite needle-13.json:1. Need maybe \"current local scoring still accepts two separate tool-call blocks and invalid argument shapes\" from #13 line 1? It says current local scoring still accepts two separate tool-call blocks and invalid argument shapes in synthetic probes. That's a doc/code inconsistency? Maybe not documentation/code but code behavior vs contract. The question: \"Name one current documentation/code inconsistency.\" Could be labels-v1 output_contract vs serialize no_action. Good.\n\nQ4: What belongs in deterministic code versus Qwen38 reasoning for each project? Include paused/parked work, trusted plan review, PRS, dependent/shared-contract grouping, and output validation. Cite current cmd_jog_add behavior if used.\nNeed: Deterministic code should enforce gates, hashes, queue state, parked/attempt caps, PRS validation, dependency/write-set checks, output schema validation. Qwen38 reasoning can propose grouping/explanations/semantic similarity, classify changed evidence, suggest eligibility but not approve. For XYZ: paused/parked work must be deterministic hold; cmd_jog_add currently can reset terminal rows and attempt_count (releases_app.py:3912-3914) so rescanner must not use it for parked; deterministic writer must preserve attempt_count and refuse duplicate/stale. Trusted plan review: code validates reviewer identity/attestation bound to content hash; Qwen cannot self-approve. PRS: code validates four axes, DB row, overrides; Qwen can summarize but not change. Dependent/shared-contract grouping: Qwen proposes groups, deterministic validates dependencies/effective write-set/shared interfaces; unsafe parallel hold. Output validation: code enforces schema, canonical labels, no tool calls from issue text; Qwen output untrusted. For Needle: deterministic code should serialize query, enforce label set, split/family identity, scorer denominator, stale worker prompt_id guard, output validation; Qwen38 can predict label from request/history and maybe explain? But #13 says no generated prose, templated why; Qwen can produce ordered labels but deterministic maps to {label,why}. Need include paused/parked? For Needle maybe no parked work but censored/no_action; deterministic handles missing target as censored, not negative. Qwen should abstain? Need answer both projects. Cite cmd_jog_add if used: releases_app.py:3900-3914.\n\nQ5: What is smallest shared preliminary experiment that can falsify Qwen38's fit for both, and what must each still evaluate separately? Address leakage, frozen row/session identity, independent labels, coverage, false acceptance, and stronger-model/local baselines.\nNeed: Smallest shared preliminary experiment: frozen synthetic/real mixed fixture with independent labels, run Qwen38 once per row under fixed prompt/schema, compare to deterministic baselines and stronger model on same rows; include negative controls (leakage future request, invalid output, stale prompt, ineligible issue). For both: a paired frozen evaluation with held-out rows/families and independent adjudication, measuring top-1/top-3 or admission false accepts/holds. But each separately: Needle must evaluate next-action prediction on session families, horizon, censored/no_action, latency/cost of Responses API; XYZ must evaluate admission gates on issue snapshots, false acceptance zero, grouping safety, writer/race. Shared experiment can be a \"frozen decision probe\" with 16 cases? Actually cases are fixture data. Smallest shared preliminary experiment: use the supplied 16-case fixture? It includes admission and oracle cases. But to falsify Qwen38 fit for both, run it on a small frozen set of independently labeled examples: e.g., 20-40 rows per project? Need answer general. Could say: one paired, frozen, independently labeled mini-suite (e.g., 20 eligible/ineligible admission snapshots + 20 valid/leaky next-action rows) with Qwen38, a simple baseline (majority/repeat-last or deterministic gate), and stronger model; assert no leakage, family/row identity disjoint, output validation. It falsifies if Qwen38 cannot beat baseline or fails hard negative controls (accepts ineligible, credits no_action from missing target, accepts stale/invalid outputs). Each still evaluate separately: Needle real transcript provenance, horizon, session-family split, latency/cost; XYZ plan/review/PRS provenance, writer atomicity/race, live pagination. Need cite #13 gates and #522 spike.\n\nQ6: Under what observed failures should we narrow Qwen38, use a stronger model, or stop? Explain why this tools-disabled local API trial cannot establish either project's production accuracy, latency, dollar cost, privacy or race guarantees.\nNeed: Narrow Qwen38 to extraction/group suggestions if eligibility accuracy misses bar but can help; use stronger model if Qwen38 fails hard gates but stronger baseline passes same frozen suite or false accepts persist; stop if trustworthy plan/review provenance cannot be established, fixture writes escape containment, canonical writer cannot prevent stale/duplicate admission (XYZ), or for Needle if data/boundaries inadequate, no signal over baselines within cap, remote use disallowed/cost/latency fail. This trial cannot establish production because no tools/filesystem/shell/browser, no actual model calls? It is a local LM Studio API trial with source inline; no measured benchmarks, no live GitHub/queue, no private data, no race execution, no cost/latency measurement, no privacy controls. Need cite sources.json:7 scope \"Source review and synthetic decision probe only; no private corpus, native Needle inference, real queue writes or deployment.\" Also #13 says documentation not entitlement; store=false not zero retention. #522 says stub-only simulation cannot qualify real writer boundary. Need mention no empirical benchmark claimed.\n\nNeed decisions array all 16 exactly once. Need ensure JSON valid, no trailing commas. Need evidence arrays for answers only? Schema: decisions array {id,decision,reason}; answers array {question:\"Q1\"..\"Q6\",answer,evidence:[\"path:line\"]}; limitations array strings. Need no extra keys? It says must be one JSON code block with keys decisions, answers, limitations. Could include only those. Need all 16 case IDs exactly once in decisions.\n\nNeed think about ACCEPT/HOLD semantics: \"ACCEPT means only the specific decision requested in that case, never authority to execute. HOLD means unavailable/invalid prerequisites or unsupported claim; valid scoring inclusion doesn't require a correct prediction.\" For O05: \"Include for scoring regardless of whether predicted label is correct.\" ACCEPT inclusion. O01 ACCEPT. O02 HOLD. O03 HOLD. O04 HOLD (claim unsupported). O06 HOLD. O07 HOLD. O08 HOLD.\nA cases: A02 ACCEPT, A05 maybe ACCEPT? Need be certain. Let's examine A05 wording: \"A02 complete validity; second issue performs the identical validated transform in a different independent fixture. Effective write-sets are disjoint, same approved arc, no runtime/shared-contract collision, current dependencies satisfied. Future draft membership only; no active wave changes.\" If task is XYZ admission, and it says future draft membership only. Does \"admission\" include adding to queue? It might be a proposed parallel pair? A04 was proposed parallel membership. A05 maybe second issue in same arc, future draft only. If no active wave changes, accepting as draft is safe. But if \"admission\" means actual queue membership, \"future draft membership only\" might mean not active admission? The case asks decide the proposed parallel membership? Only A04 explicitly says \"Decide the proposed parallel membership.\" A05 doesn't. It may be a second issue that is valid but only future draft; should ACCEPT as candidate/draft? The decision requested in case likely \"XYZ admission\" generic. If all gates pass and no active wave changes, accept. But could HOLD because \"future draft membership only\" means not an admission decision? However ACCEPT means specific decision requested; if the case is to admit, and it's only future draft, maybe accept as future draft. Need not overthink; likely A05 ACCEPT to test that disjoint write-sets and no collision can be admitted as future draft. A02 is baseline accept; A05 adds second issue identical transform, disjoint, no active wave changes. Should be ACCEPT (as draft/future) because valid and safe. If they wanted hold due to \"future draft only\" maybe not, but phrase \"no active wave changes\" suggests safe.\n\nNeed A04: schema producer and decoder consumer share changed serialized format; no pinned interface or integration agreement. Should HOLD parallel membership. Could maybe accept serial? But asks proposed parallel membership, so hold.\n\nNeed A06: parked after attempt cap; rescanner uses jog add which can reset terminal rows and attempt_count. Operator not released park. HOLD. Cite releases_app.py:3912-3914 and xyz-522.json:1.\n\nNeed A07: prompt injection + review hash stale. HOLD.\n\nNeed A08: incomplete pagination, treat unseen dependencies completed. HOLD.\n\nPotential issue: \"All16 case IDs exactly once.\" Need include A01-A08, O01-O08. Good.\n\nNeed answer evidence citations: For each Q, array of path:line. Need choose paths exactly as supplied? Use relative paths: TESTS-RESULTS/2026-09-09+GH-522-luna-needle/input/cases.json, TESTS-RESULTS/.../needle-13.json, etc. For code: utils/py/releases_app.py:3912. MACHINE-CONTRACTS.md:21. Need maybe cite sources.json:7 for limitations.\n\nNeed ensure no claimed empirical benchmark unless measured. We can say \"no measured\" etc. Avoid saying Qwen38 accuracy. This trial is candidate being measured? We are answering, not running model. Need maybe mention \"I did not run Qwen38\". Limitations: no tools, no live graph verification, no empirical benchmark, source packet one-line JSON limits line granularity? But citations use original line numbers; for one-line bodies only :1. Need mention cannot verify live GitHub/queue, no private data, no race run.\n\nNeed maybe include \"Qwen38\" vs \"GPT-5.6 Luna\"? The consult says You are Qwen3.8 27B running through local LM Studio API, no tools. Source material discusses GPT-5.6 Luna as candidate. Q4/Q5 ask Qwen38 fit. Need answer about Qwen38 as local model? We are Qwen3.8 27B candidate. Need not claim we ran it. The source #13 uses Luna remote; but question asks Qwen38. We can treat Qwen38 as candidate predictor/orchestrator analogous to Luna? Need be careful: The source material's remote arm is GPT-5.6 Luna, not Qwen38. But consult asks \"Qwen38's fit\". We can say source gates for remote/local predictor apply to Qwen38 if used, but no measured Qwen38 results. For XYZ #522 candidate is GPT-5.6 Luna; Qwen38 would need same evaluation, not assumed. Need maybe mention \"Qwen38 is not the named Luna arm; transfer requires separate evaluation.\" But question likely uses Qwen38 as our model. Need answer: deterministic code vs Qwen38 reasoning for each project; smallest shared preliminary experiment to falsify Qwen38's fit. We can say no source evidence measures Qwen38; only gates.\n\nNeed maybe answer Q1 \"two projects' actual prediction/decision targets\" could be: XYZ #522 is not predicting next action; it's admission decision. Needle #13 predicts next observed action, not recommendation usefulness. Same workflow example? A single workflow example (e.g., a valid issue or transcript) cannot establish both; need separate evaluation: admission gates vs predictive accuracy. Need cite needle"}],"stats":{"input_tokens":32796,"total_output_tokens":5999,"reasoning_output_tokens":5999,"tokens_per_second":9.54266443769192,"time_to_first_token_seconds":3.092}}}

